Z||000002||Oreif||06-09-2000||12:38 AM||||The scoop is an Indy Fiero scoop used on the REAL Indy pace cars in 1984. I bought it from IRM for $200. They come "non-functional" But as long as you don't use IRM's mounting kit and open the face it can be 100% functional. I have pics of how I mounted it and can supply exact dimensions if you should decide to get one. IRM can be contacted at 1-800-367-8423 or E-mailed at<BR>IRMFIERO@aol.com<BR>I have also heard that you can get one from the below link also. They sell the scoop and the IMSA Fiero body kit. They call the IMSA body an SD4 body and the scoop is listed at the bottom as "street air intake scoop"<BR>I don't know what they would charge for the scoop.<P> <A HREF="http://www.showcars-bodyparts.com/fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.showcars-bodyparts.com/fiero.html</A> <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 06-09-2000).]||||reg||6
